A||N||6||BlackARROW||Motor Electrical Schema please||||5||
Z||000000||BlackARROW||02-24-2001||02:45 PM||||First, I have a 85 2M4.  Btw, I changed my sparkplugs yesterday for Bosch Platinium.  I saw  somewhere on the web that they were not good for DIS Systems (on 87/88 models).  Though I use a standard system; I just wondered.  I noticed a difference accelerating, but until the motor is warm (I'd say), it doesn't idle/run smoothly.  I guess I'll have to change my wires, and distributor. How come it wasn't doing it with the old rusted sparkplug?  (NGK v-Type)<P>My main concern is that my Tachometer stopped working and would like it to work.  From time to time, it works for a run than stops again.  I was looking for the first connection, thinking about the coil's negative seemed fine, but didn't find anything there.  I found two connections I shall redo, but I don't know what they are (even though I looked in my Fiero's Guide Book).  Two days ago, trying to find my tach problem, I don't know what connection I've touched, but now my Dash's Shift-Light doesn't light up anymore.  Since the Shift-Light and Tachometer probably uses the same connection, I wasn't far.   <P>What I am looking for is a schema (or even better: pictures) of the motor's electrical system.<P>Other problem?  I've lost by backup lights.  I've checked and the lightbulbs are ok, no fuses are blown; so where should I start?<P>For an '85, it stills runs great.  I like it very much, but I look at this other GT in my garage, and would like to have one.  <P>Damn, I got many questions today:  When I accelerate as fast as it can, when reaching about 3500/4000 rpm (can't tell exactly 'cause of the tacho :P  hehe),  I hear like a scream out of the muffler.  It doesn't look like a defect or what, but I don't have a Turbo in it.  I was just wondering what it was.  Can send an mp3 of it if your really curious as me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Any interesting link or anyone who knows what I'm talking about.<P>Thanks to all<P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||02-24-2001||03:14 PM||||Let the midget out of the trunk will probably help the scream.....<P>The ECM doesn't use the tach line. It's a seperate line. you need to go over all the distributor connectors carefully. At this point you should also hook up a scanner to it. The shift light could be the bulb. could be more complicated.<P>The tach problem is likely the tach filter. Find this and unplug it. a bad filter can screw up more than the tach.||||reg||1
Z||000002||BlackARROW||02-24-2001||03:55 PM||||Thanks theogre.  <P>I'll check for that tach filter.  Probably your right.    <P>But for the muffler scream, nope..  nobody or no audio devices is in the trunk.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I thought at first that sound was coming from the air entry, but not.  I've put a mic and recorded, and went for a ride over the 4000 rpm mark. I've moved it until I got good location, and the result is the end pipe of the exhaust.  Oh well.  I just passed a Civic last night, trying to get something out of my new sparks, I downshifted into 4th gear, and there I was on the "turbo" again. hehe..  Anyway, before with the old sparkplug, it was doing it only in 1st and 2nd.  In 3rd it was very low, almost unperceptible. But last night in 4th, it was really there.  Friends told me that when they were riding behind, they could here it very clearly.  A Turbo whistles, my thing sings on the high pitch tone.<P>I'm not a Pro, I'm just wondering.<P>thanks again<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||BlackARROW||02-24-2001||04:00 PM||||Thanks theogre.  <P>I'll check for that tach filter.  Probably your right.    <P>But for the muffler scream, nope..  nobody or no audio devices is in the trunk.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I thought at first that sound was coming from the air entry, but not.  I've put a mic and recorded, and went for a ride over the 4000 rpm mark. I've moved it until I got good location, and the result is the end pipe of the exhaust.  Oh well.  I just passed a Civic last night, trying to get something out of my new sparks, I downshifted into 4th gear, and there I was on the "turbo" again. hehe..  Anyway, before with the old sparkplug, it was doing it only in 1st and 2nd.  In 3rd it was very low, almost unperceptible. But last night in 4th, it was really there.  Friends told me that when they were riding behind, they could here it very clearly.  A Turbo whistles, my thing sings on the high pitch tone.<P>I'm not a Pro, I'm just wondering.<P>thanks again<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||MrPBody||02-24-2001||04:04 PM||||I have an '85 SE 2.5.  At full throttle and high RPM (about 4000 -- what passes for high RPM in a Duke), I also hear a whistling sound, like a thin scream.  Tentatively I assume that I'm hearing intake noise, maybe whistling from the water separator.  I have never tried to verify this guess.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||BlackARROW||02-24-2001||04:12 PM||||MrPBody, I sent you that singing via e-mail.<P>Is it the same you hear?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||BlackARROW||02-24-2001||10:46 PM||||Theogre, it worked.  I'm just back from that Fiero.  I finally manage to find that Tach filter, and there I was.  One wire was loose.  So now it's reving perfectly. <P>For my new sparkplug problem, it was kindda weird.  Well I checked my wires, and the 3rd one was loose, defective I'd say.  The wire got ripped of the plug connector.  I fixed it temporarily, but I'll need to buy new wires soon.<P>I'll go for a lil ride in a short while to see how great it is now.<P>Thanks<P>||||reg||1
